Semi-realistic 3D medical-illustration still of ONE human contractile CARDIOMYOCYTE (working heart muscle cell), centered in a square 1:1 1080x1080 frame with generous margin on a clean seamless dark studio background that fills the frame edge to edge. NO border, frame, mat, vignette or letterbox bar, and NOT rendered as a picture lying on a surface. Soft global illumination, gentle rim light, subtle subsurface scattering through the translucent sarcolemma, scientific-animation look.

MORPHOLOGY: a short, stocky, roughly cylindrical striated muscle cell lying diagonally across the frame, only about five times longer than it is wide, BRANCHING into a Y at each end — the branching must be unmistakable. At the tip of each branch the cell meets a neighbouring cardiomyocyte END TO END, and every one of those contacts is a pronounced, STEP-LIKE, staircase-shaped transverse junction running right across the full width of the fibre — the INTERCALATED DISC — with interlocking finger-like relief along the step faces. The neighbours are modelled faintly, cropped by the frame edge, clearly subordinate to the central cell.

A soft translucent cutaway along the upper half reveals the interior in NATURAL, believable biological tones, clearly distinguishable, neither near-monochrome nor neon:
- parallel MYOFIBRILS with crisp regular cross-striations — deeper rose A bands alternating with pale cream I bands and a slate-blue Z-disc line in the centre of each I band, aligned in register across the cell;
- ONE oval, softly glowing blue-violet nucleus in the MIDDLE of the cell, in a spindle-shaped myofibril-free clearing;
- densely packed amber-ochre MITOCHONDRIA with modelled inner cristae, filling every channel between the myofibrils in long rows and clustering around the nucleus, plainly occupying about a third of the cell's interior;
- wide pale-blue T-TUBULES plunging in from the surface, each entering exactly at the level of a Z-disc, each hugged by a swollen terminal cisterna of the pale lilac SARCOPLASMIC RETICULUM that sleeves the myofibrils;
- at the nearest intercalated disc, teal GAP JUNCTION plaques modelled on the LONGITUDINAL step faces and small ochre DESMOSOME plaques with sage-olive FASCIA ADHERENS bands on the TRANSVERSE step faces.

DO NOT model: a long unbranched multinucleated skeletal muscle fibre; a peripheral row of nuclei against the membrane; a smooth tapered unstriated smooth-muscle spindle; neuron-like dendrites, axons, synapses or myelin; a motor end plate; a cell wall, nucleoid, plasmids, flagella or cilia; T-tubules at the A-I junction. Absolutely NO text, letters, numbers, labels, arrows, scale bars or watermarks anywhere in the image.
